# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Farmer 360 — environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in what you need:
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is GITIGNORED — passwords never land in the repository.
# Values here are read by: npm run dev / build / preview, npm run db:migrate,
# npm run db:sync, npm run db:status, ./run.sh, ./startup.sh, ./update.sh.
# A variable exported in your shell always wins over this file.
#
# DATABASE RESOLUTION (first match wins — leave everything unset to run on the
# embedded PGLite fallback, which needs no setup but resets on every restart):
#   1. DATABASE_URL below (any real Postgres: Docker, Supabase, Neon, RDS…)
#   2. A local Postgres server (./run.sh starts/initialises one in .localdb/)
#   3. Embedded PGLite (automatic fallback)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Primary database — pick ONE ──────────────────────────────────────────────

# Docker Postgres (container "farmer360-db", as created in the Codespace):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://farmer:YOUR_PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:5432/farmer360

# Supabase (Project Settings → Database → Connection string → URI):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.YOUR_PROJECT:YOUR_PASSWORD@aws-0-region.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# Neon (Connection string from the Neon dashboard):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-cool-name-123456.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# Self-hosted / system Postgres:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://farmer@127.0.0.1:5432/farmer360

# ── Multi-database setup (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Connect to MORE than one database and copy data between them:
#   npm run db:status   → shows every configured database + reachability
#   npm run db:sync     → copies schema + data from SOURCE to TARGET
#
# Example: develop on the Docker Postgres, then sync into Supabase.
# SYNC_SOURCE_URL is the database data is copied FROM, SYNC_TARGET_URL the one
# data is copied TO (the TARGET is overwritten table-by-table — use --dry-run
# first). Source defaults to DATABASE_URL when only the target is set.

# SYNC_SOURCE_URL=postgresql://farmer:YOUR_PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:5432/farmer360
# SYNC_TARGET_URL=postgresql://postgres.YOUR_PROJECT:YOUR_PASSWORD@aws-0-region.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# ── App behaviour (rarely needed) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITE_AUTH_ENABLED=true
